WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.060
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:15.727
Unit eight: Being Polite. In this unit, you will ask for things politely and show good manners.

4
00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:17.532
Polite.

5
00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:21.079
Polite means speaking and acting with good manners.

6
00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:23.599
Polite students say please and thank you.

7
00:00:24.299 --> 00:00:27.044
Your turn. Say: Polite.

8
00:00:29.744 --> 00:00:30.537
Polite.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.168
Please.

10
00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.227
Please means a word you use to ask nicely.

11
00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:36.981
Can you help me, please?

12
00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:40.090
Your turn. Say: Please.

13
00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:43.547
Please.

14
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.423
Thank you.

15
00:00:46.123 --> 00:00:48.413
Thank you means words to show you are grateful.

16
00:00:48.713 --> 00:00:49.970
Thank you for your help.

17
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.020
Your turn. Say: Thank you.

18
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.524
Thank you.

19
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:58.541
Excuse me.

20
00:00:59.241 --> 00:01:02.378
Excuse me means words you say to get attention politely.

21
00:01:02.678 --> 00:01:04.933
Excuse me, where is the library?

22
00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:08.344
Your turn. Say: Excuse me.

23
00:01:11.044 --> 00:01:12.242
Excuse me.

24
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.123
Sorry.

25
00:01:14.823 --> 00:01:17.694
Sorry means a word you say when you make a mistake.

26
00:01:17.994 --> 00:01:19.378
Sorry, I didn't see you.

27
00:01:20.078 --> 00:01:22.707
Your turn. Say: Sorry.

28
00:01:25.407 --> 00:01:26.385
Sorry.

29
00:01:27.383 --> 00:01:28.187
Interrupt.

30
00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:31.734
Interrupt means to stop someone while they are speaking.

31
00:01:32.034 --> 00:01:34.289
Please don't interrupt the teacher.

32
00:01:34.989 --> 00:01:37.049
Your turn. Say: Interrupt.

33
00:01:39.749 --> 00:01:40.843
Interrupt.

34
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:42.828
Manners.

35
00:01:43.528 --> 00:01:45.748
Manners means polite ways of behaving.

36
00:01:46.048 --> 00:01:48.210
My grandparents teach me good manners.

37
00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.609
Your turn. Say: Manners.

38
00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:55.229
Manners.

39
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:57.113
Kind.

40
00:01:57.813 --> 00:02:00.080
Kind means friendly and caring to others.

41
00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.008
It was kind of you to help me.

42
00:02:02.708 --> 00:02:05.047
Your turn. Say: Kind.

43
00:02:07.747 --> 00:02:08.411
Kind.

44
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:11.556
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:11.856 --> 00:02:14.563
Sreypich, would you mind opening the window?

46
00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:17.841
Not at all. Here you are.

47
00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:22.232
Thank you. Would you mind helping Dara with his homework?

48
00:02:23.517 --> 00:02:25.960
Of course not. I'm happy to help.

49
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.878
You have very good manners!

50
00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:34.020
Thank you, Mr. Jake. My parents taught me to be polite.

51
00:02:35.317 --> 00:02:38.477
Grammar focus: Would you mind plus verb-ing?.

52
00:02:38.777 --> 00:02:41.569
Would you mind closing the door? Not at all.

53
00:02:41.869 --> 00:02:46.550
To say yes, answer 'Not at all' or 'Of course not' — it means you don't mind!

54
00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.179
Now read and listen. Good Manners at School.

55
00:02:50.479 --> 00:02:52.479
Good manners make everyone happy.

56
00:02:53.783 --> 00:02:56.166
At school, we say please and thank you.

57
00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.170
When we need help, we say, 'Would you mind helping me?'

58
00:03:02.483 --> 00:03:04.727
We don't interrupt when the teacher is speaking.

59
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:09.456
If we make a mistake, we say sorry and try to be kind.

60
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.333
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:15.226
Would you mind blank the door?

62
00:03:15.526 --> 00:03:19.458
A, closing. B, close. C, to close.

63
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.693
The answer is A: closing.

64
00:03:27.183 --> 00:03:29.589
To stop someone while they are speaking is to blank.

65
00:03:29.889 --> 00:03:33.543
A, interrupt. B, apologize. C, listen.

66
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.712
The answer is A: interrupt.

67
00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:43.030
Polite ways of behaving are blank.

68
00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.810
A, manners. B, customs. C, rituals.

69
00:03:50.817 --> 00:03:53.095
The answer is A: manners.

70
00:03:54.583 --> 00:03:57.863
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you show good manners?

71
00:04:03.163 --> 00:04:09.022
I say please and thank you, and I don't interrupt people. When I need help, I say, 'Would you mind helping me?'

72
00:04:09.322 --> 00:04:11.112
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:16.325
Great work today! You learned eight new words and would you mind plus verb-ing?.

74
00:04:16.625 --> 00:04:19.765
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

75
00:04:20.065 --> 00:04:22.508
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

76
00:04:22.808 --> 00:04:25.669
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

